e go to our renovation filter options  we have basically a plethora of  different options and  different styles that we can choose from  adjust change as we see fit  we can graphically override every single  individual element but that's really  going into the details of arcade and  probably something you don't need to  worry about on day one but it's good to  know that this feature is available to  you if for some example you wish your  demolition line to be blue instead of  red for any particular reason if we go  and cancel out of all that and go back  to our main toolbars at the top you'll  see we have our typical toolbars at the  top file hosts everything it usually  does and you can work your way through  these  to see everything that is available to  you to be honest there isn't too many  critical things you need to know about  but i will only go through the most  important things in this toolbar that  you'll probably use in day one or at  least week one first of all open close  save save as all very basic you know how  they work you don't have to have them  explained libraries and objects and  library manager this one is probably one  of the most critical if you're importing  any external libraries if your company  has libraries that they're importing  into the project if you're starting work  for a brand new company and have never  used archived before this is definitely  something you're going to need to know  it's very critical all you have to do is  go add find that folder with the  libraries import it and arcad will do  the rest now coming back out of that and  going to our info section under file and  project info  the project info basically dictates  everything about the project in a very  simple and organized manner if we type  in the project name the description the  project id or any of these details down  here we can simply replicate them later  on by producing auto text  that is very very useful to anybody  doing a title block it means they don't 